Configure it from GitHub Copilot Chat instead
In the Copilot Chat panel on the right:
Make sure the lower-left mode says:
text
Agent
Click the small Tools / sliders icon at the bottom of the Copilot Chat box, next to Auto.
Look for one of these options:
text
Configure MCP Server
Add MCP Tools
Manage MCP Servers
Open that option from Copilot Chat, not IntelliJ Settings / Agent Customizations.
Copilot should open an MCP configuration file.
Copy the entire content of your local:
text
.fnb-etaf\copilot\mcp.json
into the Copilot MCP configuration file.
Save it.
Reload/restart Copilot Chat if it asks.
After that, open Copilot’s Tools list. You must see:
text
fnb-etaf-playwright-local
Only then is GitHub Copilot connected to the local Playwright MCP server.